  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Finely chop the onion. Crush or finely chop 1 garlic clove. Discard the tough inner stems from the kale, then thinly slice the leaves. Pick the mint leaves, discarding the stems. Drain and rinse the lentils.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/282576/photos/large/prep_ingredients-15ff559a228b1fd79274298648f255d1.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook onion: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Add the onion, season with salt and pepper and cook, stirring occasionally, for 4-5 mins until softened.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/282577/photos/large/cook_onion-ef56c4b0d8f2661d59528a9caed6098d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add curry powder: Add the garlic, 3 tsp Malaysian curry powder (see Make it yours) and 1 tbs tomato paste to the onion. Cook, stirring, for 1 min or until fragrant.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/282578/photos/large/add_curry_powder-a9f7cccf6f95b9ac67e4a0333d1bf6df.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer soup: Reserve 2 tbs coconut milk to serve. Add the remaining coconut milk, tomatoes and 625ml (2½ cups) boiling water to the pan and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to medium and cook for 10 mins or until slightly reduced.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/282579/photos/large/simmer_soup-18f309846ca35cdf5f5940008e5e9177.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the kale and lentils to the soup and cook, stirring, for 2 mins or until the kale is wilted. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the soup among bowls, drizzle with the reserved coconut milk and scatter over the mint. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/282580/photos/large/serve_up-ee410be5726378d61b3bf138f418538e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: This soup has a lovely gentle heat, but if you'd like it milder, just reduce the curry powder. If you'd like more heat, scatter over chilli flakes to serve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/282581/photos/large/make_it_yours-ba1fc544002c44a4e5607a1e1699172a.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
